@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+requires "reference-semantics/semantics.k"
+
+module SAME-CHARS-BODY-MUTATED
+  imports MPY
+
+  syntax KItem ::= "#sameCharsBodyMut" "(" IntSeq "," IntSeq ")"
+
+  // Deliberately false source-body mutation: compare set(s0) with itself.
+  rule <k> #sameCharsBodyMut(S0:IntSeq, S1:IntSeq)
+        => Call(
+             closureVal(
+               ("s0", "s1", .ParamNames),
+               (Return(
+                  Compare(
+                    Call(Name("set"), (Name("s0"), .Exprs)),
+                    CmpOp("==",
+                      Call(Name("set"), (Name("s0"), .Exprs)))))
+                .Stmts),
+               0),
+             (str(S0), str(S1), .Exprs))
+           ...
+       </k>
+endmodule

The claim is satisfiable and result-constraining; KAST comparison pins the exact translated body, ground instances agree, and a material executed-body mutation builds but produces the expected unmet-obligation residual. The exhaustive 931-record K inventory is preserved and the used rule slice has no oracle or execution bypass.
  ✓ Read required Kit skills and validate launcher/provenance integrity
  ✓ Check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Rebuild semantics/proof from clean scratch and rerun all positive claims
  ✓ Audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and satisfying instances
  ✓ Inventory and review every K declaration and rule for soundness
  → Create and run a fresh meaningful non-vacuity mutation
  • Account for assumptions/trust boundaries and write REVIEW.md with verdict
